   rows from several versions interleave. The shared Refresh button keeps
   calling the existing `loadDomainRuns()`.
2. `src/front/templates/dtwin.html` — Added a second, page-level
   `analyticsRunDetailsModal` (with `analyticsRunDetailsBody` for the JS to
   fill) immediately after the existing `runDetailsModal`, following the
   same page-level placement rule that modal's comment documents: a modal
   inside a hidden `.sidebar-section` shows its backdrop but never its
   dialog.
3. `tests/units/front/test_runs_page.py` (new) — Upgraded the brief's
   file-read-only test approach to the stronger pattern already used by
   `tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py`: drive a `TestClient` against
   `GET /dtwin/` and parse the rendered HTML with its `_html` / `_tags` /
   `_find` helpers (imported directly — `tests/units/api/__init__.py`
   exists). 10 of 14 tests assert on rendered HTML — every build/analytics
   element id, the version filter's absence from the served page, the
   analytics table's column headers, the modal's presence, and that the
   Refresh button's `onclick` is still exactly `loadDomainRuns()`. Rendered
